{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1087567-what-trade-languages-would-uktena-and-wendigo-use","id":1087567,"title":"What Trade Languages would Uktena and Wendigo use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T01:10:38-07:00","id":1087567,"title":"What Trade Languages would Uktena and Wendigo use?","content":"So doing a Wild West Game, and two of the characters were never human, being Lupus and Metis Uktena. We had the lupus choose Mojave as the language he learned. But I'm asking what do you think the main trade languages the Uktena and Wendigo used 200-500 years ago. Do you think the Pure Tribes made use of a particular language so much, that they would regularly learn it even far away from its native speaker population?<br /> <br /> These are native american languages I am asking about, not European ones like Spanish and English.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T01:59:18-07:00","id":1087576,"title":"","content":"Navajo was the predominant language spoken by the Natives of the American south west at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:47:54-07:00","id":1087590,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much that is helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T04:03:01-07:00","id":1087613,"title":"","content":"Chinook wawa, classical Nahuatl (though that ended fairly shortly after European settlement), Tutelo, Chipewyan (depending on the time and area would have been more wide spread than Navajo from the Dene languages)... there's a lot of possibilities. There wasn't every really one big trade language that would have made sense for the Pure Ones to adopt as a primary one, but you could probably narrow it down to 3 or 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:01:33-07:00","id":1087628,"title":"","content":"Curious did you have to look that up or did you just know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:23:08-07:00","id":1087887,"title":"","content":"Both?<br /> <br /> I mean, I've been playing WtA for a long time, and the Uktena are one of me favorite Tribes, and one of my old regular gaming people is active in Native rights in the Americas politics, so I've picked up a bunch of that over the years. But I also looked it up to make sure I didn't recall anything incorrectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}